255:''A gate that forgets a denial admits the withdrawn vessel again'', so what a sovereign gate learned outlives a restart. It rests in the gate's own vessel store, sealed under the vessel key behind the vessel's one store door, and on no board another operator reads.
260:* ''It passes the registry test'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/registry-filter#/the-test">>): each event stands authored by its subject's own hand, the gate reads it as of its own last learning, and the store offers no enumeration.
262:* ''A fresh vessel knows nothing'', and accepts as a gate that learned nothing accepts (#/named-leaks), until the first honest vessel of a face dials it.
263:* ''A store rolled back forgets.'' Every event in an older copy of a row still verifies, so a hand that restores one makes the gate forget what it learned since. No fence here stops that hand; the next honest vessel of the face teaches the gate again.
268:| a gate that learned nothing newer, facing the withdrawn vessel | that gate accepts the withdrawn vessel under the admitted face | the first honest vessel of that face to dial the gate; nothing else in this proof |
269:| a withdrawn vessel that shows an older frontier | nothing at a gate that holds the denial: the denial names its key whatever frontier it claims. At a gate that never learned, the row above | the same |
270:| a relay or a herm that withholds | nothing: the history rides inside the encrypted exchange between a presenter and the gate | |
293:''A session opens before its certificate'' (operator ruling, approved as presented). The vessel's own chain verifies first: the face key, its certificate, this vessel's face-scoped key, with no learned denial. The face supplier joins THAT to the admit and the private grant, and the owner opens the session wearing the face. Only then does the signer mint the session's key and its certificate under the vessel's face-scoped key. The owner answers no caller between the two acts: one door opens the session and mints its signer, and a mint that fails closes the session it opened before any message routes to it. No session ever stands live with a face and no signer.
316:''The sibling-facing proof moves to face scope together with the herm-facing stamp.'' The channel seals a face-scoped session proof and the face-private membership authority to its sibling, and binds its Repo peer id to the proven face session. It transmits no device delegation and derives no peer id from a device key. The herm stamps the separate per-dial relay identity alone.
318:''Each face holds its own group secrets, channel tags and actor ids.'' No identifier at the vessel's level reappears through a lower layer: an actor id, a sibling peer id, a channel tag or a presentation lineage shared across two faces would rebuild the link the proof removed.
347:* ''The subjects'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/face-proof-subjects.ts`): the typed keys, the scope, the certificate and its request, the withdrawal event, the frontier, the session certificate, every signed image, and a reader for each. Every key and signature passes the one door (`ed25519-door.ts`); the purposes stand in the domain table (`domains.ts`).
350:* ''The gate bundle'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/gate-bundle.ts`): the floor and sovereign tiers with their typed routes and roots (the serving tier stands owed with the ember's train E), the pin, its digest, the knock, the prologue, and the transport and signing keys one gate derives per (tier, Nexus, route). Nothing rests. Its caller: the vessel's gate composer.
363:* ''The floor and sovereign roots' doors'' stand at their seats (the serving key's door stands owed with train E), and no composer calls them until the socket cutover. A floor bundle asks the floor key's derive door (`vesselFloorKeyDoor`, `packages/lararium-node/src/node-vessel-identity.ts`), which answers while the vessel rests locked, hands back a fresh child its caller overwrites and never the floor key. A sovereign bundle asks the custody seat's (`custodyGateDoor`, `packages/lararium-node/src/custody-seat.ts`), which answers only while the seat holds its key. The two doors carry two types, so a line that hands one tier's door to the other fails to compile; a root refuses a door of the other tier and a door no mint made by name (`door-other-tier`); and each seat's door refuses the other tier's child by name. A door states only what its minter claimed, so one weld holds the minters to the two seats: a second caller of either mint, anywhere in source, turns it red (`packages/lararium-node/tests/gate-root-door-minters.test.ts`). The composer owes the call.
372:* ''The sealed frames' layout'': the frame that carries the gate's handshake reply, and the frames that carry a presentation, a frontier and the events beside it. They ride binary WebSocket messages no proxy reads; the layout in `gate-exchange.ts` stands as the house's own; the cutover has landed, and roadmap row `W28` freezes it before the founding bake.
373:* ''The withdrawal proof under a live partition.'' The fold and the six verdicts stand proven as pure functions over synthetic histories, and the six answers stand proven at one gate against a dialer in the same process, partitioned by hand. No two gates and no real herm have yet carried one.
382:# ''Sibling carriage.'' The herm dial, the inner proof and the sibling peer id move to face scope.

