bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/live-equivocation.mem:60:Real cabals with real stakes do not exist yet, so abstract unit tests cannot feel the tension the mechanics must survive. ''The fiction serves as the first QA environment.'' Telarus the wild-mage lit Elyncia's DreamNet ~500 years before modern day (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/characters/primary-characters/telarus">>), and 500 years of rise · dormancy · revival · betrayal · inheritance give a scenario library to RUN the mechanics against. A cabal name grafted across generations; a wild-mage's DreamNet identity live-hijacked mid-working; a shrine-realm slept a century then woken for a rite; a Dread-Pirate-Roberts-style name presented by a rotating crew — each makes a load-bearing user story for the ahi-kā reading, the handle-KEL, the recovery-quorum, and this exposure. The `AHI_KA_500YR` defaults (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ahi-ka">>) stand calibrated to this world; tune them by running its events. ''irl tension + fiction series = the QA env.''
