bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor.mem:196:''There stands no second KIND of Herm.'' A crossroads nobody has raised and a hearth whose archive holds shut rest in the same state, and naming them apart freezes a difference that does not survive contact: ''anyone who can raise a vessel at the floor may raise it on arrival.'' On Elyncia this reads as the ordinary thing rather than the exception — a wayside marker gets a building raised over it and a hearth fire lit when somebody comes to dwell, and the marker never stood as a different kind of thing from the house. Gaia's own crossroads shrines grew the same way.
