bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:82:# ''The presentation follows in the first encrypted frames.'' A face's presentation carries the face's public key, the vessel's face-scoped key with its certificate, the session key with its certificate, ONE presentation arm (an admit, a hosting grant, or an invite claim) and that arm's causal lineage, and the presenter's withdrawal frontier with any events the gate may lack (#/the-withdrawal-proof). An admit's `nym` MUST equal the face key. No ContactCard, no vessel key, no persona root, no root edge, no identifier shared across faces, and by default no Handle rides it.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:84:''The admit's signed bytes carry the canon-document list and a validated full `GateBundlePin` for the hearth's sovereign sync route at its named Nexus. `readGateBundlePin` reads the object and its digest derives from it; the quorum's salted `carriageCommit` binds the opening inside the act image. A joinee reads the opening only through the admit at its held root (`verifySignedAdmitBundle`). Floor routes receive separate full pins through an authenticated relation or signed pin set; a floor announcement cannot authenticate its own first pin. `device-admit.ts` mints the internal `device-admit/v1` edge, and the fleet answer carries the pin and canon list.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:105:* ''Whether a hosting grant or an invite claim holds stays the sorter's own reading.'' The gate binds the arm to the face key and the Nexus, and attaches a walker only where the sorter read one.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:318:''Each face holds its own group secrets, channel tags and actor ids.'' No identifier at the vessel's level reappears through a lower layer: an actor id, a sibling peer id, a channel tag or a presentation lineage shared across two faces would rebuild the link the proof removed.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:360:* ''The admit's own mark.'' The supplier reads the presenter-verifier's verdict over an admit and checks it against the chain. The admit's quorum signs a commitment to what it carries (`carriageCommit`), and the held-root door hands back the head of the admitted nym's key line, which the supplier holds against the chain's face key; the verdict itself still carries no mark a caller cannot spell by hand. A chain another vessel presented verifies as well as this vessel's own, so the session opener also owes the supplier the key its own custody row names.
