bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:56:* ''The docker mesh'' (by hand): `crossing-witness`; `node tools/mesh-pins.mjs --up` stands the mesh pinned; `herm-mesh-witness` carries `node/alpha` across three hops; `mesh-scenarios nexus` (`tools/mesh-scenarios.sh --list` names every scenario and starts no build; `MESH_PROJECT` names the run's own compose project). The mesh publishes `MESH_PORT_*` on loopback, every node service requires `LARES_HARNESS_IMAGE`, and `tools/harness-image.sh` checks its digest. A hearth whose log carries a `[lararium] fatal:` line reads as not stood.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:132:* ''Introduction and admission'': a user introduces; an operator admits; the answer consumes the introduction (operator ruling).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:160:* ''A herm answers the knock.'' A charterless herm answers any proven peer that knocked (`ownPlacePosture`): a waystone by class, never a broken lararium. A lararium reads its charter, and an absent or torn charter reads PRIVATE.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:203:* ''One Keyhive identity per PersonaGroup, none above them'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18: //"it's the only way to retain control over faces that don't know about each other"//). Each face's PersonaGroup owns its Keyhive identity, its event store, its registry, its archive and its content-key seat; no vessel-wide identity registers a face's bags, delegates them, or holds a face's group. Two faces of one vessel then never link on the wire, a removal from one face rolls that face's bags alone, and a bundle restores one face and nothing of another. Today the vessel's own identity registers every bag and delegates each face's bags through itself, and the vessel and every face share one event store and one content-key holder (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/keyhive-per-persona-group-2026">>). House readings under the operator's confidence, each naming what flips it: a herm keeps a floor-only transport key, behind a red test that it can neither author, resolve nor observe a face's capabilities, and holds no Keyhive identity if that test fails; several face hives share one process only after a substrate probe reads them isolated, and each face's hive runs in its own worker otherwise; co-mingled history migrates by fresh identities and an old mixed archive refuses by name, with no bridge; a founder that cannot leave its group leaves by a fresh PersonaGroup. Row `K15` carries the build, folding `W25` and `K12`; `W26`'s slice 3 waits on its face context.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:243:* ''Routes at the cutover'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). Walker arms, the sibling dial and the herm membership relay ship SHUT by name; H opens walkers with its live grant reader, W9 opens the sibling at face scope, and an explicit Nexus opens the herm relay. The oracle read face and reader convert where browser boot reads the oracle in production; elsewhere they ship SHUT by name after measuring `pullAndVerifyOracle`'s caller. The waystone reads the Nexus's one public answer before it trusts its engine. An untested old-wire fallback counts as open. The reason: a closed route grants no silent legacy authority. The ruling flips on a proven gate-native caller for each shut route.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:338:* ''The hosting rows'': a hearth's hosting state, each spend and its walkers' carriage rest as HOT rows sealed under the VK, in the storage home of the custody seat (`packages/lararium-node/src/hosting-store.ts`, `hosting-carry.ts`). The sealed writer writes a whole file and appends to none, so each spend lands as ONE row of its own, named by a digest of its nonce or marker: the row's presence IS the burn, and it reads, decides and seals under one custody holder. The spend row commits a redemption, and what rides ahead of it re-derives: the grant from the epoch, the leaf, the nonce and the claim, so a crash before the answer replays as `retry`; the operator's counts from the rows standing, by name. A roll's state row commits the roll, and the hosting doc re-derives from it: the next roll and each sovereign stand land an act the sealed state holds and the doc lacks (`landHostingActs`). The sweep of dead epochs' rows passes through the seat's removal door (`removeCustodyRow`), which removes only a row this vessel's key opens; a spend that sealed after a roll retired its epoch burns nothing live and leaves with the next sweep. Each carried value rests as one row whose name carries its address and its length, so a guest's bytes read off its rows and no counter stands beside them. One process serves a hearth's carriage (the standing vessel's own gate, under its store claim), and its contacts and deposits run in turn, so a quota reads the bytes the last deposit left and a reclaim never discards on a reading a contact moved meanwhile. A row that stands and does not open refuses by name: a burn nobody can read never reads as unspent, and a carried value nobody can open never reads as absent. A floor composition reads no hosting row, so a locked hearth sorts no socket as a walker. `lares host`, `host roll` and `host invite` ride the custody door (`host.state` · `host.roll` · `host.invite`): a minted invite as a verb's outcome would rest in the daemon's document in the clear.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:374:* ''Per-dial transport keys on the sibling channel'': a leaf proves to a herm under a key fresh per dial, and the leaf-peer transcript binds that key in place of the device key the relay stamps, so a herm colluding with a revoked leaf reads no sibling's device key off its own gate (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/identity-slot-policy#/the-persona-group-secret`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:459:* `K15` One hive per face (#/rulings, 2026-10-18): each PersonaGroup owns its Keyhive identity, event store, registry, archive and content-key seat, and no identity stands above them. Build order, each step red-first: (0) before bytes move, the custody contract of <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero">>: the node and browser row census sorted D, F or S, the FCK key class, each face's own slot tree and recovery route, the carrier binding of face, row name and kind, and the overwrite contract generalized to a row-class key (#/rulings, a face's custody rows seal under its own key; a shared act never makes a shared secret) (the node census built, PR #70: each carrier row names its target classes, a LEAD mark and its open joint, and `encodeCarrierContext` spells the D and S seal context; the archive-row-selector joint traced and held open, PR #71: no archive site hands its row an authenticated PersonaGroup); (1) a substrate probe that two Keyhive instances in one process hold apart under interleaved acts, a reboot and a cross-read (measured: isolation holds, `packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/two-hives-one-process.probe.test.ts`), then a face context with its own store, registry, archive and key seat; (2) the face as the sole owner of its identity and group, the vessel's delegation gone from every face-bearing event (built, PR #68: `makeFaceBagDoor`, `faceOwnerVerifier`, a two-face event-byte capture its red, `W25`'s probe its regression), and 2b, a bag keeping one Document across boots (built, PR #68: `registerBagsDurably`, its record on the daemon doc for the vessel's ground and on each face's plane for that face's bags); the door grants the face's group before it records a Document (PR #69), so a crash between them re-enters to the same end; (2c, operator ruling 2026-10-19; built, PR #79) the atom cut: a random atom per (vessel, PersonaGroup) under that face's FCK signs every act on the face's behalf on node and browser, the place signer keeps the floor's duties alone, the wire subjects and verifiers move together, and its genesis, admit and founding-bootstrap deltas ride `X0` by `genesis/unbaked.json`, red-first on a thief holding the place seed deriving no veil and opening no group secret; on the local presence channel the session wears the mounted face, so a verb's presenter derives from the island's own atom and never from the CLI's unsigned `requestedBy`, the floor presents the place for floor acts alone, and a verb that names another face refuses by name (#/rulings, a session wears the face, 2026-10-11; a published atom key would link face and vessel on a wire); (3) sessions and registries routed by one face, no union, with `F6` slice three's asker-seals beside it, each sealer holding its row class's key (built, PR #81: the browser house keys by (PersonaGroup, persona root), the island proves each face through `gate:clear` while the holder holds no key, the island reads the fleet board's dyad itself, a fresh group mints a fresh atom, founding seeds key by their ask digest, and the node keys its atom and veil-archive rows by PersonaGroup digest; the daemon's last unions ride step 6); (4) content keys and removal per face, `K12`'s fresh group inside it; (5) a one-face restore and a herm that carries yet authors nothing; (6) the fence migration, identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, and archive and custody formats together, under one identity model (#/rulings, sync carries, verification decides: the sealed anchor, the signed `@persona` log, verified projections): each D row (the atom's seed, its archive) seals under its face's FCK, where the node now seals them under the seated vessel key, and keys by its PersonaGroup, as the node's atom and veil-archive rows and the browser's atom row already do, where the browser's veil archive still keys by handle index. The isolation red: unlock face A alone, bypass every route, and try to open and replace B's occupied carriers with every key A holds, the VK included; each open fails, B's bytes stand unchanged, and A's bundle restored on a fresh vessel holds nothing of B. Lead: DreamNet-Wright after `W26`'s floor slice lands. K, W. Wave C (step 6 under the identity anchor, `readFace` as the one door with its census) landed in PR #86 on 2026-10-23. Wave D (the FCK fence, kit `docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane`) and `K15-H` (the Handle owner rides the anchor, the row in `docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane`) build beside each other; `K17`'s realm leg (`docs/pono/k17-realm-lease-lane`) follows Wave D.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:483:* `K16` The Teshima Family Council (#/rulings, 2026-10-18; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm">>), `K15`'s acceptance story. Kalani founds a private council; Leilani joins it with two of her three faces. Red-first, after `K15`'s face context: (1) the council's hive as a Keyhive group holding no key of its own, its members the chosen faces' own identities; (2) an invite walks Leilani to the door, the threshold grafts each chosen face, a face leaves by its own act, and another's removal rides `kapae` or a fork by omission; (3) a member face's photo lands in its working layer of the council wiki and reaches the council's canon by `MOVE` (`W27`); (4) both chosen faces read it, the face kept back reads nothing and learns nothing, and no event in the council's history names a creator or issuer that ties two of Leilani's faces together; (5) a herm carries the sealed book and authors nothing (`K15` step 5). The e2e set stands four vessels: Kalani's, one per chosen face of Leilani's, and a herm. The e2e set walks the council at one hearth first: Kalani's seed charter holds the realm and Leilani's chosen faces walk there as guests, no Nexus founded (#/rulings, one charter). The two-hearth council follows, under the Nexus the two found, and there the member consult that lets a realm's documents cross between two operators reads a root map nothing fills (cabal-realm #/many-realms, owed), and the climb from seed charter to Nexus re-pins the realm by a named act (owed). Open joints: a quorum Handle with a seated key stands only where the council signs as one name, and that key signs collective acts alone, reaching no member's hive (#/the-steward-signer, owed). K, W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:489:* `W12` The herm route for cancel and the three receipts, as ruled (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/receipt-ledger#/the-relay-leg">>); no code asks, cancels or answers across a herm. Owed, with `W9`: the ask, the cancel and the vessel's answer as a tagged inner frame under the sealed sibling session's own seal, the vessel reading that session's proof as the asker's; the herm's bare delivery note inside the session, bound to the ask's unique request id and the session's causal position, attesting transit and never execution; and the rule for which verbs a sibling's standing reaches across the session (`sibling-channel.ts`, `uds-channel.ts`). W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:519:* `P10` The vessel-side fetch door stands built (`makeCidResolver` beside `hermCasTransitFromEnv` in `open-node-vessel.ts`); the herm's own client leg waits on the explicit-Nexus herm relay, since a herm dials no hearth. One circle in the law stands beside it: a carrier may read a book its registration declares public, the declaration lives on the realm doc, and the realm doc never crosses to a carrier. The held red in `tests/e2e/herm-reshares-public-blob.e2e.test.ts` waits on both. Also owed: seeding a herm from a stood Lararium. House. Before the fence where the ceremony seeds a herm.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:590:* `W24` `herm-reshares-public-blob` walks a public user book (PR #55): the fleet mints `herm-public-photo` on A and registers it public on the realm; step ③ LOADs the blob into the book's working slot and promotes it into canon by `MOVE` through the island `W27` opens; step ④ reads C, a second vessel of A's own face joined by `fleet join`, listing the book with A's doc id through its stood realms; steps ⑤b and ⑦ name an unstaged blob, and ⑦'s shut holds. Owed beside: readiness entries (a wiki mounted with its layers laid) and a per-carrier entry, so a script awaits a second write too; the daemon's reach waits on a bag's document the way the kernel's slot wait does, instead of one bounded find; a guard on the event route's order; a CLI that gives up on its budget cancels its waiter. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:662:* `W18` The founding hearth's carriage fold walks the roll anchors (PR #50): after a charter roll, the carrier folds at the carriage pull's refresh, `placeCarriedNexuses`, the membership refold and the carry-bundle take count every act the anchored lineage carries, and count none without an anchor (`carriageAncestryFromBoard`; red and controls in `carrier-fold-across-roll.test.ts`). Held-out herm-mesh and the nexus cell then read A filing all four pins and verifying relay-2, and with `P20`'s gate half (PR #54) both read green. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/l-space.mem:46:The ''dead sink below'' names thermodynamic equilibrium — the static fixed point a relation //relaxes into// when it freezes. A bare `X ${copula} Y` reads as a trajectory sliding downhill: it fuses a live relation into static identity, draining toward dead water. ''The copula is the gradient down; L-Prime is the through-flux that holds the center metastable'' above its own sink. The discipline reads thermodynamic, not merely stylistic: cut the active-voice flux and the address relaxes into essence-static, the center falling into the sink.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/identity-enacts-relation.mem:232:''And the young-Cabal case has an answer:'' //"we can use the presence of individuating mechanisms to infer whether the objects at a hierarchical level have the capacity, EVEN IF THE CAPACITY IS NOT CURRENTLY BEING REALISED."// Mechanism-presence carries modal force where an activity metric carries none — a quiet island still holds standing. ''And the capacity stays parasitic on a history of actual EXERCISE'' — mechanism-presence grounds it, and nothing grounds it absent acts, which separates YOUTH (holds, merely recent) from LAPSE (holds gone) without stipulating either. Worked at thirteen centuries by Ise shikinen sengū: //the stored object never reads as the building; it reads as the capacity to re-stand the building, kept alive only by mandated exercise// (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/pattern-integrities-cultural">>, P7).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/system-pattern-integrities.mem:377:desc  = "The test, run against every threshold: name its outward face, name its inward face, and ask what lets one leak into the other. Leaks this law catches: a host-minted stub that lets a guest's lineage follow her out and names her; a cleartext vessel seed or persona root standing beside the floor; a walker syncing the whole carriage board, which puts the Nexus's infra graph on a guest's face; a herm asked to speak as a house, which puts a household's face on a waystone. One leak recurs at every threshold that carries a party across it: a NAME on the outside. The outside carries only what its reader already holds or resolves — a bearing to an address, or the reader's own out-of-band pin — and a party's identity rides only inside the span a check or a proof covers. Hence a carrier's heading reads `from=\"?\"` and its authorship begins after STX (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/memetic-wikitext-framing#/bearing-arrow`), and the wire never names the gate key a dialer proves to — the dialer's pin, which Noise IK carries as its `<- s` pre-message (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/siege-resilience#/the-active-prober`). The release's `-> to=\"?\"` hands the initiative back (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot#/causal-islands`) and answers a different question; THR_5 governs the gate's silence and not the carrier."
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/local-first.mem:71:through a herm that reads none of it (`tests/e2e/leaf-sibling-sync.test.ts`). The browser
