bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:195:* ''The system wikis release; every other wiki reads the floor'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-16). Only each Nexus's Kahu cabal writes the `lares` and `lararium` wikis and bags live. Every other wiki, and every other hand, mounts them read-only by CID: the latest release that cabal approved. The release rides the Nexus's crossroads board as its public answer, naming the floor CID under the Kahu steward's seal. The cabal approves the exact bytes under its charter's threshold, and a herm carries the answer without signing it. Every wiki mounts that floor through `@oracle`, which never writes. A vessel moves its floor pin only when it accepts a newer signed release. With no Nexus speaking, it stands on its last accepted floor, or on genesis. A face's wikis follow the floor of the Nexus that face stands in, so one vessel may hold two floors and never ties its faces together. An edit aimed at the floor copies up into the wiki's own working layer, and an offering back travels as a draft into the cabal's realm. A lone hearth is a Nexus of one, so its operator stands as its own Kahu. Row `W26` carries the build.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:208:* ''Custody and identity read by capability, never by host'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19: //"I consider node and browser isomorphic-by-intent. Eventually, a browser-vessel somewhere may grow comparable capabilities to a node vessel, and this pattern cascades outwards to all future vessels."//). Three rules hold on every vessel, present and planned: a vessel meets each face through that face's atom alone, its veil signing every dial, join, enrolment, sibling channel and daemon proof made on that face's behalf, never one device-wide key; a vessel holds a place signer exactly while it stands a floor, for the floor's allowlisted duties, under the pre-rotated place KEL; and a faceless vessel reading another's floor proves nothing private, reading the public shelf under the floor card's pin. A node's daemon auth, device-key signer, sibling enrolment and group-secret opener read the one vessel seed today (`open-node-vessel.ts`), and a browser's do the same (`open-browser-vessel.ts`); each is a bond owed, carried by `K15`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:214:* ''One owner per registry; the floor reads by CID'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18: //"Architecture stands, leans stand"//). The `@oracle` document as a registry every vessel writes retires: one id carried one `lares` and one `lararium` pointer for the whole fleet, and a joined vessel's pointer replaced its hearth's, a shape a two-vessel probe and three shard runs measured. `@oracle` stands as the floor's read-face over a manifest CID, which a wiki mounts read-only by the pin its face accepted. Each registry carries only what its scope's owner writes: a vessel's bootstrap holds its own document pointers and its accepted floor pins; `@catalog` the operator's documents; the Kahu realm the live `lares` and `lararium` documents and their drafts; the crossroads board the Nexus's one public answer. The leans the ruling adopts: the Kahu realm holds the live system documents, with `bags/` projected on the Kahu's vessel alone; a one-seat founding lands a counted 1-of-1 Kahu-cabal admission for persona zero's group, so one predicate decides every hand's reach into system canon; the release answer, the Nexus's one public answer, names the Nexus AID, the charter epoch, the release before it and the floor manifest CID, sealed by the steward, with the promotion approval over the manifest's exact bytes riding attached; a vessel records an accepted release as a sealed hot row per (face, Nexus) that only a person's act moves; genesis bakes the first floor, a corpus CID in the seed. A signing domain of its own carries the release, `floor-release`, so no seal over another shape verifies as one (operator-approved, 2026-10-18). The shape and its slices stand at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane">>; rows `W26`, `W21` and `P8` carry the build.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:219:* ''The ember's serving gate'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). A third gate tier, the serving route, takes its bundle from SK, and the floor and sovereign tiers stand untouched; a pin moves only by a signed causal event or a verified key-history step, and no quiet period ages a pin out. The reason: a dialer that pinned the sovereign tier never mistakes a serving hearth for an unlocked one. The ruling flips on proof that a gate pin decides no authority anywhere (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:230:* ''Engine cadence'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). Cadence keeps its own lineage and threshold, apart from every seat key. A Nexus's joint founding cites one cadence inception that names each founder's hearth, the device that bears the reboot, as a holder; a household seed carries none, since its one holder bears its reboots. Each hearth mints its cadence key at random on the device, never derived from serving or floor material, and keeps it, with its next-key commitment, as a `cold` row under the vessel key that unwraps per act; no sixth custody class and no extra card at the founding. A holder may later rotate onto a cold card by its own choice. Each island pins one engine epoch, and one daemon hosts two epochs only as two separately pinned islands. The reason: the people who bear a reboot decide it, and a seat-holder who runs no hardware forces no one's restart. The ruling flips on a cadence act that must run unattended where a per-act unwrap cannot (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/contract">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:244:* ''The floor announcement'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). `waking-floor-announce` signs one canonical body per carried Nexus under that Nexus's floor bundle signing key: version, Nexus AID, floor route pin digest, floor standing and causal position. It travels only inside an authenticated socket or relay relation. The reader checks the already pinned floor pin, domain, Nexus, route and causal order, and treats the body as a peer hint alone. The reason: a floor hint must neither bootstrap its own trust nor replay across Nexuses. The ruling flips on a smaller body that still refuses cross-Nexus replay, stale replacement and first-contact self-certification.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:335:* ''The vessel-identity family'': the persona roster, the worn-face selector, the pet-name map, the declaration map and the published-face record rest sealed under the VK as hot rows; each persona root rests as a cold row, opened for one act; the floor vessel key rests beside its signed inception, every load proves that inception, and no next-key seed or commitment rides it. The roster commits a root: a mint writes the root row, then the roster line that carries the root's public key, so a reading of a public key answers off the hot roster and opens no root. A root row with no roster line reads as an orphan: no reader holds it, `lares persona list` names it, and the same mint run again adopts it. A roster line whose root row went missing, or names another key, refuses by name at the act that needs the seed, and nothing mints over it. A hot row with nothing at its path reads as holding nothing; a row that stands and does not open, or opens to another shape, refuses by name at every read and every write. A vessel key mints only inside a held custody, and lands with its inception under the custody's one claim: the key file commits the mint, so two acts never commit two keys, and a boot loads a key and never mints one. The floor reads no row of the family, so a carried-Nexus reading by persona (a seated chair, a kept consent) answers empty until the key arrives, and a sovereign composition reads the roster whole before it stands (`packages/lararium-node/src/node-vessel-identity.ts`). A floor composition reads no roster, so it shuts every fleet lane: it sorts every device as set aside, sets a proven sibling aside, and its fetch door reads no peer as fleet, the pinned join gate's key included (`packages/lararium-node/src/floor-fleet-lanes.ts`). It still folds the one fleet board its own device edge names in the clear, so the Binding Gate reads this vessel's own seat at every standing.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:337:* ''The walk records'': each hearth a vessel walks at keeps one HOT row sealed under the VK, named by a digest of that hearth's gate key (`packages/lararium-node/src/node-walk-store.ts`). A record holds bearer invites, the hearth's grant and one receipt per carried document (`{ cid: "blake3:<hex>", ref, key }`, whose `key` opens that document), so it counts as a secret row. The row rests in the storage home of the custody seat: the store takes no directory, so no caller files it beside a document store the vessel key never spans. Nothing at a hearth's path reads as no walk there; a row that stands and does not open, opens to another shape, or rests filed under another hearth's name refuses the read, the list and the update by name, and an update seals a whole record or nothing. Each change reads, decides and seals under one custody holder, so one invite leaves a wallet once. A floor composition reads no walk record and presents no walk; a fresh browser device stands at the floor under its `#floor=` card, and a joined face crosses under its root-signed pin. A key that locks under a live walk costs the walk one message, which it logs. `lares walk`, `walk take` and `walk invite` ride the custody door (`walk.state` · `walk.take` · `walk.invite`): a carried invite as a verb's argument, or an invite as a verb's outcome, would rest in the daemon's document in the clear.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:369:* A per-Nexus wire key in two tiers (operator ruling): a floor route's bundle derives from the floor key and answers at a locked vessel; a sovereign route's bundle derives from the sealed custody root and stands only while the vessel stands unlocked. One gate per (Nexus, route), so knock, pin, verdict and posture read per Nexus exactly (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>). The serving route's third tier rides train E (`E3`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:506:* ''Integrity owed: the floor's trust chain'' (`W14`, `W15`, `W16`: the signed floor card, the pin's causal position, carry-floor convergence). Its witness: a rotation-and-carry storm that accepts no stale pin and converges the same way on every carrier.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:512:* `W14` The floor card a banner carries in its `#floor=` link reads unsigned, on origin trust; a signed card stays owed. The floor read by release (`W26` slice 4) adds one rung and closes nothing here: a browser holding the Nexus AID verifies the epoch lineage, the head release and the floor bytes itself (`browser-floor-read`), anchored to the AID alone, since the genesis epoch re-derives it. The lineage rides the release record and the porch answer, never the card (a card holds 4096 characters, and the lineage self-certifies); that carrier changes nothing about trust, because the AID that anchors it comes from the card or the genesis CID the reader already pins and never from the answer, and an answer self-consistent for another AID refuses (`floor-answer.test`). The AID itself still rides the same-origin trust line, and nothing proves the card's freshness: the signed card (`W14`), the pin's causal position (`W15`) and the carry-floor convergence (`W16`) stay owed for anchoring the AID and the card. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:513:* `W15` A floor pin statement carries no causal position, and `hearthPinIndex` files first-wins, so a rotated floor key re-files only on restart (`admit-gate-pin.ts`, `place-floor-pin.ts`). W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:514:* `W16` Two-vault carry: the carry partials land no floor pin, so a cofounded Nexus carries no herm yet (`nexus-contract.ts`). W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:663:* `W21` A joinee mounts the hearth's `@lararium` corpus read-only beside its own, while the oracle plane never crosses (#/rulings, 2026-10-16). Each vessel's pointers rest in its own `@catalog` (PR #52), so a joined vessel's pointer no longer replaces its hearth's, and `shared-oracle-doc.probe` holds that two synced vessels each keep their own. The rest rides `W26`'s floor slices: a joinee reads its hearth's floor by the release and its CIDs (slice 4), where slice 5's accept act moves its pin; a sibling device of a seat-holding face reads the floor until Wave C's face context carries the charter and the board to it, and `device-admit.ts` states the law. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:725:# ''Built'': fleet join on every face carries a device edge, face certificates, grants, a sealed address secret, the charter, the household admit and the floor pins; the admit and fleet answer sign the full sovereign sync route pin after N's cosign door.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:726:# ''Built'': every vessel socket follows attach, verdict and open through the sealed face gate; one dial per (hearth, Nexus) off the admit's pin; the floor announcement signs under its pinned gate bundle; a fresh browser device stands at the floor; a herm answers the knock where a Nexus carries it.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:50:| Gate bundle | the gate derives separate, domain-separated transport and signing keys per (tier, Nexus, route): a floor route's from the floor key, a serving route's from the serving key, a sovereign route's from the sealed custody root (#/the-gate-exchange) | nowhere: a bundle lives in memory from a derivation to a drop; a dialer pins it per (Nexus, route) | the dialer, and anyone handed the pin |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:84:''The admit's signed bytes carry the canon-document list and a validated full `GateBundlePin` for the hearth's sovereign sync route at its named Nexus. `readGateBundlePin` reads the object and its digest derives from it; the quorum's salted `carriageCommit` binds the opening inside the act image. A joinee reads the opening only through the admit at its held root (`verifySignedAdmitBundle`). Floor routes receive separate full pins through an authenticated relation or signed pin set; a floor announcement cannot authenticate its own first pin. `device-admit.ts` mints the internal `device-admit/v1` edge, and the fleet answer carries the pin and canon list.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:114:''A route names its tier, and a tier names its root.'' A ''floor route'' answers at a locked vessel: the public shelf, the oracle's read face, the floor's announcement, and a herm's blind relay of bytes it cannot open. Its bundle derives from the floor key. A ''sovereign route'' seats a face's session, syncs a private document or serves a lane whose bytes this vessel can open. Its bundle derives from the sealed custody root, and it exists only while the vessel stands unlocked. A route's typed name carries its tier, the pin states it and the pin's digest binds it: no route asks the other tier's root, a root asked for the wrong tier refuses by name, and a dialer that pinned one tier believes no gate of the other.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:116:''Each derivation takes the tier, the Nexus and the route under its own name.'' No pin, key, digest or knock of one tier, one Nexus or one route links to another for an outsider: one vessel's floor pin and its sovereign pin for one Nexus share nothing.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:122:''A floor gate seats no fleet lane.'' It asks no private grant and sorts nobody same-operator, it reads no withdrawal memory and answers no refusing state, and it marks every seat it opens as the floor's, so that seat reaches the public shelf and what the floor serves, and nothing this vessel can open. A presenter that asks more dials the sovereign route, and finds no gate there while the vessel rests locked. A floor route a design adds keeps this law: the ember's route (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ember#/the-raise">>) seats a dialer by the transport key a standing ember pin names, and no device of the person's fleet by its fleet key.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:128:''A serving route answers at a vessel its embers raised to SERVING'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ember">>): the serving gate for presenters already standing, and blind carriage for them. Its bundle derives from the serving key under its own registered domain, and it exists only while the vessel stands at SERVING or unlocked. The floor and sovereign tiers stand untouched: no serving route asks the floor key or the custody root, and a dialer that pinned the sovereign tier believes no serving gate. A serving gate signs its own handshake and no act, and its seat reaches what the serving tier holds and nothing beyond it.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:350:* ''The gate bundle'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/gate-bundle.ts`): the floor and sovereign tiers with their typed routes and roots (the serving tier stands owed with the ember's train E), the pin, its digest, the knock, the prologue, and the transport and signing keys one gate derives per (tier, Nexus, route). Nothing rests. Its caller: the vessel's gate composer.

